    "description": "AdaptOrDeity's starting organism: generic_adaptive_cell empty_membrane plus the proteins of a ~2 um prokaryote in a Proterozoic sea (pH 7.3) that makes its ATP by homolactic fermentation and spends a quarter of it on an F1Fo H+-ATPase, which pumps protons out and so powers the membrane potential and the other ion gradients. Each protein is a protein_pool (its expression, costs, daughter share and membrane area) and the module it scales: i_flagellum (i_H_flagellum MotAB: the proton-driven flagellar motor; one flagellum at start), i_H_ATPase (FoF1, 10/3 H+ per ATP), i_NaH (NhaA, 2 H+ in per Na+ out), i_KH (KefC, K+/H+), i_K_Trk (i_leak_K adaptive as the Trk K+ uptake channel), i_NaCa (adaptive; archaeal NCX_Mj is the prokaryotic equivalent) and membrane_face (cell_membrane_face adaptive: the Glf glucose facilitator and a lactate-/H+ symporter). The default instance is an exact steady state at -105 mV and pH 7.6 with total ATP turnover equal to Lynch & Marinov's maintenance cost at 20 C. Three glucose carriers the game unlocks after level 1 sit beside Glf with their pools at 0 (m_init and m_target 0), so the level-1 cell is unchanged until the game sets a target: glc_PTS (glucose_carrier ATP, instance PTS: the phosphotransferase system, Km 5 uM, one PEP charged as one ATP per glucose), glc_ABC (instance ABC: binding-protein importer, Km 0.5 uM, 2 ATP per glucose) and glc_GalP (glucose_carrier H_symport: Km 0.1 mM, one H+ per glucose). Each takes its medium glucose from its own C_glc_e parameter, set to the same value as membrane_face's.",
